      },
      "worked": "Fix the unique V. The remaining letters have $4!\\div(2!2!)=6$ orders relative to it: LLEE, LELE, LEEL, ELLE, ELEL and EELL.\nFlipping reverses the order. LLEE and EELL form one pair; LELE and ELEL form another. LEEL and ELLE each equal their own reverse and give two further arrangements.\nThus the number of distinct bracelets is $2+1+1=4$.",
